  "id": "COMPOUND:16783 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Flavipin may interact with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through a series of molecular pathways involving thioredoxin, diplotrin A, and micaolide J. These compounds are all targets of Flavipin, and each of them is associated with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 in different ways. Thioredoxin, mitochondrial is directly targeted by Flavipin, and its interaction with the transporter is supported by the evidence. Diplotrin A and micaolide J also target the same transporter, indicating that Flavipin may influence the transporter through these intermediates. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible mechanism by which Flavipin could modulate the function of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. The evidence supports a potential regulatory role of Flavipin in the transporter, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
